# Export API Rules

All FiveM exports registered via `src/api/registerExports.ts` and handler modules must follow the response envelope pattern:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
try {
  const result = await db.collection(name).insertOne(doc);
  return { success: true, insertedId: String(result.insertedId) };
} catch (error) {
  return { success: false, error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : "An unknown error occurred" };
}

// ❌ BAD — CTFFramework has no try/catch
throw new Error("Database not connected");
```

Required field semantics:
- `insertedId`: always `string`
- `update`: include `modifiedCount` from MongoDB driver
- `delete`: include `deletedCount` from MongoDB driver
- `find` not found: `{ success: true, data: null }` (aligned with `findById`)

After export changes: update `docs/API.md` and run `yarn build`.
